  },
  data: {
    LLM: "In the dealer-as-banker form, each non-dealer player is resolved in turn. Dealer reveals first card, then second card for that player. Player may fold or bet up to the pot limit. Dealer reveals third card and settles: strictly between = win amount equal to bet, outside range = lose bet, equal to an endpoint = lose double ('hitting the post').",
    Player: "In the dealer-as-banker form, each non-dealer player is resolved in turn. Dealer reveals first card, then second card for that player. Player may fold or bet up to the pot limit. Dealer reveals third card and settles: strictly between = win amount equal to bet, outside range = lose bet, equal to an endpoint = lose double ('hitting the post').",
    objective: 'Win bets by correctly calling that the third card falls strictly between the first two card ranks.',
    gameplay: "In the dealer-as-banker form, each non-dealer player is resolved in turn. Dealer reveals first card, then second card for that player. Player may fold or bet up to the pot limit. Dealer reveals third card and settles: strictly between = win amount equal to bet, outside range = lose bet, equal to an endpoint = lose double ('hitting the post').",
    keyRules: [
      'Third card strictly between first two ranks is a win.',
      'Third card outside interval is a loss.',
      'Third card equal to an endpoint commonly loses double (hitting the post) in many rulesets.',
      'Consecutive first two cards usually produce a push in several versions.',
      'Pair starts are handled by special house payout rules.',
    ],
